   As others have already posted, but I feel like reiterating: Wishing is 
/supposed/ to be a sort of exact science, for at least two reasons (not 
counting the pansy reason that drop-down menus aren't trivial to implement 
in text mode):

   (1) A menu of "closely matching" items amounts to a humongous spoiler.
A newbie might not know that he could wish for a oyrffrq fvyire qentba 
fpnyr znvy, or a gva bs jbbqpuhpx zrng, and he might not want the game 
to spoil him by revealing those items' existence.

   (2) IMHO, Nethack is a game for smart people who like to get things 
right, and wishing is a powerful /incentive/ to get things --- such as 
spelling --- right. I certainly don't think wishing for a "ring of fire 
resistence" ought to get you a ring of fire resistance, any more than 
wishing for "gray draggon skalemale" should get you GDSM. Nethack rewards 
correctness in English spelling, as well as patience and strategy and 
whatnot. This newsgroup is one of the most literate groups I read, 
despite many --- most? --- of the regulars' having English as their
second language. I credit Nethack for that. ;)

   That said, I /would/ like to see the wish parser recognize more 
(correctly spelled!) variations on item names. "Helm" versus "helmet" 
seems like a good one. And as an r.g.r.n reader, I'd like to see "GDSM" 
and "rubber chicken" make it into the parser's lexicon. :)  Does anyone 
have any more additions they'd like to see?  I might cook up a patch, if
there are enough additions to make it worthwhile.

